{
  "name": "Multi-Website Uptime & Latency Monitor with History, Telegram & Email",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "7ebbf1c6-f537-496b-a838-239ca1e05abd",
      "name": "Setup Guide",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 680,
        "content": "## Website Uptime Monitor \u00b7 Setup guide\n\n**1. Enter websites**\nOpen **Configure Website List \u2192 Parameters \u2192 websites**. Keep the field name `websites`; enter domains or URLs separated by commas or newlines. Example: `example.com, https://example.org/health`.\n\n**2. Choose optional alerts**\nOpen **Monitor Settings**. For Telegram, enable the channel, set `telegram_chat_id`, and include the same ID as a string in `telegram_allowed_chat_ids`. Select your bot credential on **Send Telegram Alert**. For email, enable the channel, fill the sender/recipient, and select an SMTP credential on **Send Email Alert**. Store passwords only in Credentials.\n\n**3. Test and activate**\nRun **Run Monitor Now**, inspect the execution, then publish/activate for checks every 5 minutes. Missing tables are created automatically. A first healthy check or unchanged state sends no alert.\n\n**Maintenance**\n**Setup Tables Once** is optional. To delete old history, set **Cleanup Settings \u2192 retention_days**, then run **Cleanup History**. Deletion is permanent.\n\n**Usage**\nUse one copy per project and avoid overlapping runs. Increase the interval for large or slow lists. Delivery failures appear in **Notification Delivery Failed**; they are not queued for later delivery.\n\n**Import this file into a new, empty workflow.** Importing into an existing canvas adds another set of nodes."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
